\par 1. If your expression does contain NO brackets:
\par 
\par 
\par  1. -Create yourself or find a table with the priority of the tokens:
\par 
\par      For example, use this table:
\par 
\par        ----------------------
\par        Token         Priority
\par        ----------------------
\par 
\par        #             0
\par 
\par        -             1
\par 
\par        +             1
\par 
\par        *             2
\par 
\par        /             2
\par 
\par        a, b, c, ...  3
\par 
\par        digits        3
\par 
\par        ----------------------
\par 
\par  2. -Create a stack
\par 
\par      1. Put the special token '#' on the
\par         stack. This will serve to mark
\par         the empty stack.
\par 
\par  3. -While not at the end of the expression
\par 
\par      1. read the next token from the expression
\par 
\par      2. if this token has a GREATER PRIORITY
\par         than the last token on the stack,
\par         push its value on this stack
\par 
\par         else
\par 
\par      3. if this token has a SMALLER OR EQUAL PRIORITY
\par         than the last token on the stack
\par 
\par         1. remove all stack tokens
\par            with a priority higher or equal
\par            than that token, and put
\par            this removed tokens at the end
\par            of the result.
\par 
\par         2. after that push that token on the
\par            stack
\par 
\par  4. -Endwhile: Go back to step 3.
\par 
\par  5. -If the expression becomes empty, and you
\par      are finished, remove and output all
\par      the remaining tokens (except the special
\par      '#' token) from the stack.
\par      Put these tokens at the end of the result.
\par 
